-# `build-from-source`: builds SDL3 from vendored source as part of the Rust build (via `cmake`
-# + a C/C++ toolchain, both already required for other native deps here) instead of the crate's
-# own default of requiring a pre-installed system SDL3 via pkg-config/vcpkg -- keeps this
-# self-contained/versioned by Roves, the same reasoning `docs/DEPENDENCY_REVIEW.md` already
-# applies to the rest of the embedded engine, and avoids a second native-installer saga on top
-# of GStreamer's (see CUSTOMIZATIONS.md).
-# `raw-window-handle`: lets `sdl3::video::Window` implement `HasWindowHandle`/`HasDisplayHandle`
-# (confirmed real, per-platform implementations in the crate's own source, not just a
-# feature-flag guess) -- `surfman`'s GL context creation needs exactly this trait, the same way
-# it currently gets it from `winit::window::Window`. Part of the SDL3 windowing/event-loop
-# migration (see TODO.md) -- unused until `headed_window.rs` actually switches its window type.
-sdl3 = { version = "0.20", default-features = false, features = ["build-from-source-static", "raw-window-handle"] }
